{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cguupz9M1p9URD1UhcEKb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BkBdcJR2XAvmZrQoVeTaq1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git status && git log --oneline -3 && cat .pose/roadmaps/pose-shared-runtime.md | head -80","description":"Show status and read roadmap"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14625,"cache_read_input_tokens":5626,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14625},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"1836bb20-9b3e-43fd-9ba9-8b575ace6b6d","timestamp":"2026-11-10T20:53:34.857Z","request_id":"req_011CguupytTexgZyoxFKjgcr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BkBdcJR2XAvmZrQoVeTaq1":{"command":"cd /var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2553958348/worktree && git status && git log --oneline -3 && cat .pose/roadmaps/pose-shared-runtime.md | head -80","description":"Show status and read roadmap"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01BkBdcJR2XAvmZrQoVeTaq1":{"cwd":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2553958348/worktree"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BkBdcJR2XAvmZrQoVeTaq1","type":"tool_result","content":"Not currently on any branch.\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\n80b49143 fix: the resident memo key holds the effective Git configuration; the ADR is accepted for the delivered scope\nff6cd828 Merge branch 'main' of https://github.com/oseiaspereira88/pose\n2c59cdb2 chore: record the delegated review of bounded isolated graph caches\n---\nslug: pose-shared-runtime\nstatus: draft\ncreated_at: 2026-10-13\ndepends_on:\n---\n\n# Roadmap: Domínio e runtime comuns com desempenho qualificado\n\n**Resultado:** operações CLI/MCP coerentes e custo controlado por produtor,\ncom reuso limitado e runtime opcional somente após qualificação de identidade,\ncoerência, autorização e recuperação. Consultar a [matriz](../results/pose-implementation-plan.json)\ne a [análise de performance](../reports/2026-10-12-pose-front-08-resident-performance.md).\n\n**Estado (2026-11-10):** os quatro milestones estão fechados com revisão independente\n(B32 operation-performance, B31 common-domain-handoff, B33 bounded-graph-caches e B35\noptional-worktree-runtime, esta em três fatias medidas), com o runtime opt-in e standalone\npreservado. O que o roadmap não entrega (cota e afinidade de CPU, limites por comando,\nnamed pipe no Windows, roteamento dos checks para o runtime por padrão) está em specs\nrascunho próprias, fora deste roadmap. A revisão do roadmap é feita sobre o estado congelado deste commit (sem mudar a matriz de validação nem a política até o fechamento). A chave do memo residente passou a conter a configuração efetiva do Git (revisão do roadmap, achado F1).\n\n## Milestone: operation-performance\n- after: spec:pose-check-spawns-fewer-git-processes, spec:pose-attention-within-a-second\n- target_start:\n- target_due:\n- specs: pose-governance-operation-performance\n\n**Exit gate:** B32 mede por produtor e reusa catálogo/bundles/Git por operação,\ncom clustering fiel e benchmark isolado que retém verdict/ambiente e não desfaz\narquivos do operador. Consultar o [lote 7](../reports/2026-10-13-pose-batch-7-authoring.md).\nB32 é raiz independente de B14/B15; desempenho não autoriza gates sobre dados stale.\n\n\n## Continuação prospectiva — lote 14\n\nConsultar o [lote 14](../reports/2026-10-14-pose-batch-14-authoring.md) e o\n[ADR de domínio/runtime Proposed](../adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md).\nResolver interface/IPC/ownership/compatibilidade e budgets antes de start.\nB31/B33 não exigem B35; runtime consome ambos após seus demais pré-requisitos.\n\n## Milestone: common-domain-handoff\n- after: spec:pose-cli-mcp-operation-results, spec:pose-writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication, spec:pose-governance-read-view-generation, spec:pose-recoverable-closeout-plan, spec:pose-mcp-active-context, spec:pose-safe-validate-orchestration\n- target_start:\n- target_due:\n- specs: pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff\n\n**Exit gate:** B31 preserva resultados/erros/authority por fonte de domínio comum;\nwrappers extraídos não spawnam POSE. P04 tem route/context compatível ou limitação\nexplícita; MCP oferece plan read-only/handoff tipado, conservando P15. Writes\nmantêm prova/coordenação e Harness não é substituído por execução arbitrária.\n\n## Milestone: bounded-graph-caches\n- after: spec:pose-index-generation-integrity, spec:pose-governance-read-view-generation, spec:pose-delivery-integrity-index-compaction\n- target_start:\n- target_due:\n- specs: pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches\n\n**Exit gate:** B33 conserva grafo/filtragem com isolamento profundo, mutation/race\ne redução medida de alocações/RAM; bytes/pins/waiters têm orçamento por worktree\ne global. Misses coordenadas produzem uma vez por chave; nenhuma contaminação,\nexpansão total desnecessária ou cache de autorização stale. Git reader fica scoped.\n\n## Milestone: optional-worktree-runtime\n- after: operation-performance, common-domain-handoff, bounded-graph-caches, spec:pose-git-and-dispatch-snapshot-integrity, spec:pose-cli-mcp-operation-results, spec:pose-writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication, spec:pose-index-generation-integrity, spec:pose-governance-read-view-generation, spec:pose-attention-within-a-second\n- target_start:\n- target_due:\n- specs: pose-optional-worktree-runtime, pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache, pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement\n\n**Entrega (2026-11-10):** as três fatias estão fechadas (`pose-optional-worktree-runtime`,\n`pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache`, `pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement`), com as duas\nspecs de engine que as medições pediram (`pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once`,\n`pose-governance-audit-skips-pure-git-reads`); o estado entregue e onde ele se afasta do ADR está na\núltima emenda do ADR, e a medição em `.pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.md`.\nNão entregues: cota e afinidade de CPU e limites por comando (o runtime limita o que admite e guarda).\nMedição: quatro execuções, a quarta qualifica (T1 a T7 passaram). O fechamento do milestone revisa o estado final dos três specs membros.\n\n**Exit gate:** B35 qualifica handshake user/worktree/Git/engine/schema, endpoint\nprotegido, lifecycle/restart/update e fallback CI/standalone. Stdio não é IPC\ncompartilhável; watcher é hint, writers publicam geração e efeitos ambíguos exigem\nreceipt antes de retry. CPU/jobs simultâneos preservam query/QoS/output determinístico","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"01cb7fbc-9f64-42d0-ab7c-2f11e1022b59","timestamp":"2026-11-10T20:53:35.392Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Not currently on any branch.\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\n80b49143 fix: the resident memo key holds the effective Git configuration; the ADR is accepted for the delivered scope\nff6cd828 Merge branch 'main' of https://github.com/oseiaspereira88/pose\n2c59cdb2 chore: record the delegated review of bounded isolated graph caches\n---\nslug: pose-shared-runtime\nstatus: draft\ncreated_at: 2026-10-13\ndepends_on:\n---\n\n# Roadmap: Domínio e runtime comuns com desempenho qualificado\n\n**Resultado:** operações CLI/MCP coerentes e custo controlado por produtor,\ncom reuso limitado e runtime opcional somente após qualificação de identidade,\ncoerência, autorização e recuperação. Consultar a [matriz](../results/pose-implementation-plan.json)\ne a [análise de performance](../reports/2026-10-12-pose-front-08-resident-performance.md).\n\n**Estado (2026-11-10):** os quatro milestones estão fechados com revisão independente\n(B32 operation-performance, B31 common-domain-handoff, B33 bounded-graph-caches e B35\noptional-worktree-runtime, esta em três fatias medidas), com o runtime opt-in e standalone\npreservado. O que o roadmap não entrega (cota e afinidade de CPU, limites por comando,\nnamed pipe no Windows, roteamento dos checks para o runtime por padrão) está em specs\nrascunho próprias, fora deste roadmap. A revisão do roadmap é feita sobre o estado congelado deste commit (sem mudar a matriz de validação nem a política até o fechamento). A chave do memo residente passou a conter a configuração efetiva do Git (revisão do roadmap, achado F1).\n\n## Milestone: operation-performance\n- after: spec:pose-check-spawns-fewer-git-processes, spec:pose-attention-within-a-second\n- target_start:\n- target_due:\n- specs: pose-governance-operation-performance\n\n**Exit gate:** B32 mede por produtor e reusa catálogo/bundles/Git por operação,\ncom clustering fiel e benchmark isolado que retém verdict/ambiente e não desfaz\narquivos do operador. Consultar o [lote 7](../reports/2026-10-13-pose-batch-7-authoring.md).\nB32 é raiz independente de B14/B15; desempenho não autoriza gates sobre dados stale.\n\n\n## Continuação prospectiva — lote 14\n\nConsultar o [lote 14](../reports/2026-10-14-pose-batch-14-authoring.md) e o\n[ADR de domínio/runtime Proposed](../adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md).\nResolver interface/IPC/ownership/compatibilidade e budgets antes de start.\nB31/B33 não exigem B35; runtime consome ambos após seus demais pré-requisitos.\n\n## Milestone: common-domain-handoff\n- after: spec:pose-cli-mcp-operation-results, spec:pose-writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication, spec:pose-governance-read-view-generation, spec:pose-recoverable-closeout-plan, spec:pose-mcp-active-context, spec:pose-safe-validate-orchestration\n- target_start:\n- target_due:\n- specs: pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff\n\n**Exit gate:** B31 preserva resultados/erros/authority por fonte de domínio comum;\nwrappers extraídos não spawnam POSE. P04 tem route/context compatível ou limitação\nexplícita; MCP oferece plan read-only/handoff tipado, conservando P15. Writes\nmantêm prova/coordenação e Harness não é substituído por execução arbitrária.\n\n## Milestone: bounded-graph-caches\n- after: spec:pose-index-generation-integrity, spec:pose-governance-read-view-generation, spec:pose-delivery-integrity-index-compaction\n- target_start:\n- target_due:\n- specs: pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches\n\n**Exit gate:** B33 conserva grafo/filtragem com isolamento profundo, mutation/race\ne redução medida de alocações/RAM; bytes/pins/waiters têm orçamento por worktree\ne global. Misses coordenadas produzem uma vez por chave; nenhuma contaminação,\nexpansão total desnecessária ou cache de autorização stale. Git reader fica scoped.\n\n## Milestone: optional-worktree-runtime\n- after: operation-performance, common-domain-handoff, bounded-graph-caches, spec:pose-git-and-dispatch-snapshot-integrity, spec:pose-cli-mcp-operation-results, spec:pose-writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication, spec:pose-index-generation-integrity, spec:pose-governance-read-view-generation, spec:pose-attention-within-a-second\n- target_start:\n- target_due:\n- specs: pose-optional-worktree-runtime, pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache, pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement\n\n**Entrega (2026-11-10):** as três fatias estão fechadas (`pose-optional-worktree-runtime`,\n`pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache`, `pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement`), com as duas\nspecs de engine que as medições pediram (`pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once`,\n`pose-governance-audit-skips-pure-git-reads`); o estado entregue e onde ele se afasta do ADR está na\núltima emenda do ADR, e a medição em `.pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.md`.\nNão entregues: cota e afinidade de CPU e limites por comando (o runtime limita o que admite e guarda).\nMedição: quatro execuções, a quarta qualifica (T1 a T7 passaram). O fechamento do milestone revisa o estado final dos três specs membros.\n\n**Exit gate:** B35 qualifica handshake user/worktree/Git/engine/schema, endpoint\nprotegido, lifecycle/restart/update e fallback CI/standalone. Stdio não é IPC\ncompartilhável; watcher é hint, writers publicam geração e efeitos ambíguos exigem\nreceipt antes de retry. CPU/jobs simultâneos preservam query/QoS/output determinístico","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BkBdcJR2XAvmZrQoVeTaq1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cguupz9M1p9URD1UhcEKb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y6TF8dGUYgHNCrd9RgcBWt","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2553958348/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14625,"cache_read_input_tokens":5626,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14625},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"01ae5c22-1ca6-415c-ae57-c044c9946870","timestamp":"2026-11-10T20:53:35.426Z","request_id":"req_011CguupytTexgZyoxFKjgcr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Y6TF8dGUYgHNCrd9RgcBWt":{"file_path":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2553958348/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y6TF8dGUYgHNCrd9RgcBWt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tpackage pose\n2\t\n3\timport (\n4\t\t\"container/list\"\n5\t\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n6\t\t\"encoding/hex\"\n7\t\t\"os\"\n8\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n9\t\t\"strings\"\n10\t\t\"sync\"\n11\t\t\"sync/atomic\"\n12\t)\n13\t\n14\t// ResidentGitMemo keeps, in a process that outlives one operation, the output of the Git reads\n15\t// that are pure functions of object ids or of the commit HEAD named when they ran (see\n16\t// governancePureGitRead). It is off unless a process turns it on, so nothing changes for a\n17\t// command that runs once; the optional worktree runtime turns it on (spec\n18\t// pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache). A hit is the answer Git would give: the key\n19\t// holds the commit and the shallow state, and the output of such a read cannot differ for them.\n20\ttype ResidentGitMemo struct {\n21\t\tmu      sync.Mutex\n22\t\tmax     int64\n23\t\tbytes   int64\n24\t\tentries map[string]*list.Element\n25\t\torder   *list.List // front is the most recently used\n26\t\thits    atomic.Int64\n27\t\tmisses  atomic.Int64\n28\t}\n29\t\n30\ttype residentGitEntry struct {\n31\t\tkey    string\n32\t\tstdout []byte\n33\t}\n34\t\n35\tvar residentGit atomic.Pointer[ResidentGitMemo]\n36\t\n37\t// EnableResidentGitMemo turns the memo on with a byte budget for what it retains.\n38\tfunc EnableResidentGitMemo(maxBytes int64) *ResidentGitMemo {\n39\t\tm := &ResidentGitMemo{max: maxBytes, entries: map[string]*list.Element{}, order: list.New()}\n40\t\tresidentGit.Store(m)\n41\t\treturn m\n42\t}\n43\t\n44\t// DisableResidentGitMemo turns the memo off and drops what it held.\n45\tfunc DisableResidentGitMemo() { residentGit.Store(nil) }\n46\t\n47\t// ResidentGitMemoStats are the hits, misses, entries and retained bytes since it was enabled.\n48\tfunc ResidentGitMemoStats() (hits, misses int64, entries int, bytes int64) {\n49\t\tm := residentGit.Load()\n50\t\tif m == nil {\n51\t\t\treturn 0, 0, 0, 0\n52\t\t}\n53\t\tm.mu.Lock()\n54\t\tdefer m.mu.Unlock()\n55\t\treturn m.hits.Load(), m.misses.Load(), len(m.entries), m.bytes\n56\t}\n57\t\n58\t// residentGitKey names a read: the root, the commit it was made at (empty for a read by object\n59\t// id), the shallow state of the repository and the exact command. A root whose Git directory\n60\t// is not a plain .git directory is not memoized: its shallow state is not read here. The key\n61\t// also holds the digest of the effective Git configuration of the root.\n62\tfunc residentGitKey(root, head, config string, args []string) (string, bool) {\n63\t\tif config == \"\" {\n64\t\t\t// The effective Git configuration could not be read: nothing is memoized.\n65\t\t\treturn \"\", false\n66\t\t}\n67\t\tgitDir := filepath.Join(root, \".git\")\n68\t\tinfo, err := os.Lstat(gitDir)\n69\t\tif err != nil || !info.IsDir() {\n70\t\t\treturn \"\", false\n71\t\t}\n72\t\t// The shallow file and the repository config are small: their content, not a timestamp,\n73\t\t// is part of the key.\n74\t\tdigestOf := func(name string) string {\n75\t\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(gitDir, name))\n76\t\t\tif err != nil {\n77\t\t\t\treturn \"-\"\n78\t\t\t}\n79\t\t\tsum := sha256.Sum256(raw)\n80\t\t\treturn hex.EncodeToString(sum[:8])\n81\t\t}\n82\t\tshallow := digestOf(\"shallow\")\n83\t\t// config is the digest of the effective Git configuration of the root (system, global, user,\n84\t\t// repository, worktree and command-line scopes, includes followed): any of them can change\n85\t\t// what a read answers (log.follow, for one), and the digest is taken once per operation.\n86\t\treturn strings.Join([]string{filepath.Clean(root), head, shallow, config, strings.Join(args, \"\\x00\")}, \"\\x01\"), true\n87\t}\n88\t\n89\tfunc (m *ResidentGitMemo) get(key string) ([]byte, bool) {\n90\t\tm.mu.Lock()\n91\t\tdefer m.mu.Unlock()\n92\t\tel, ok := m.entries[key]\n93\t\tif !ok {\n94\t\t\tm.misses.Add(1)\n95\t\t\treturn nil, false\n96\t\t}\n97\t\tm.order.MoveToFront(el)\n98\t\tm.hits.Add(1)\n99\t\treturn append([]byte(nil), el.Value.(*residentGitEntry).stdout...), true\n100\t}\n101\t\n102\tfunc (m *ResidentGitMemo) put(key string, stdout []byte) {\n103\t\tsize := int64(len(key) + len(stdout))\n104\t\tm.mu.Lock()\n105\t\tdefer m.mu.Unlock()\n106\t\tif size > m.max {\n107\t\t\treturn\n108\t\t}\n109\t\tif el, ok := m.entries[key]; ok {\n110\t\t\tm.bytes -= int64(len(el.Value.(*residentGitEntry).key) + len(el.Value.(*residentGitEntry).stdout))\n111\t\t\tm.order.Remove(el)\n112\t\t\tdelete(m.entries, key)\n113\t\t}\n114\t\tfor m.bytes+size > m.max {\n115\t\t\tlast := m.order.Back()\n116\t\t\tif last == nil {\n117\t\t\t\tbreak\n118\t\t\t}\n119\t\t\te := last.Value.(*residentGitEntry)\n120\t\t\tm.bytes -= int64(len(e.key) + len(e.stdout))\n121\t\t\tm.order.Remove(last)\n122\t\t\tdelete(m.entries, e.key)\n123\t\t}\n124\t\tm.entries[key] = m.order.PushFront(&residentGitEntry{key: key, stdout: append([]byte(nil), stdout...)})\n125\t\tm.bytes += size\n126\t}\n127\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"e3e891e1-edd3-4b8e-8f53-0099fedf718b","timestamp":"2026-11-10T20:53:35.435Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2553958348/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go","content":"package pose\n\nimport (\n\t\"container/list\"\n\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n\t\"encoding/hex\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"sync/atomic\"\n)\n\n// ResidentGitMemo keeps, in a process that outlives one operation, the output of the Git reads\n// that are pure functions of object ids or of the commit HEAD named when they ran (see\n// governancePureGitRead). It is off unless a process turns it on, so nothing changes for a\n// command that runs once; the optional worktree runtime turns it on (spec\n// pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache). A hit is the answer Git would give: the key\n// holds the commit and the shallow state, and the output of such a read cannot differ for them.\ntype ResidentGitMemo struct {\n\tmu      sync.Mutex\n\tmax     int64\n\tbytes   int64\n\tentries map[string]*list.Element\n\torder   *list.List // front is the most recently used\n\thits    atomic.Int64\n\tmisses  atomic.Int64\n}\n\ntype residentGitEntry struct {\n\tkey    string\n\tstdout []byte\n}\n\nvar residentGit atomic.Pointer[ResidentGitMemo]\n\n// EnableResidentGitMemo turns the memo on with a byte budget for what it retains.\nfunc EnableResidentGitMemo(maxBytes int64) *ResidentGitMemo {\n\tm := &ResidentGitMemo{max: maxBytes, entries: map[string]*list.Element{}, order: list.New()}\n\tresidentGit.Store(m)\n\treturn m\n}\n\n// DisableResidentGitMemo turns the memo off and drops what it held.\nfunc DisableResidentGitMemo() { residentGit.Store(nil) }\n\n// ResidentGitMemoStats are the hits, misses, entries and retained bytes since it was enabled.\nfunc ResidentGitMemoStats() (hits, misses int64, entries int, bytes int64) {\n\tm := residentGit.Load()\n\tif m == nil {\n\t\treturn 0, 0, 0, 0\n\t}\n\tm.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer m.mu.Unlock()\n\treturn m.hits.Load(), m.misses.Load(), len(m.entries), m.bytes\n}\n\n// residentGitKey names a read: the root, the commit it was made at (empty for a read by object\n// id), the shallow state of the repository and the exact command. A root whose Git directory\n// is not a plain .git directory is not memoized: its shallow state is not read here. The key\n// also holds the digest of the effective Git configuration of the root.\nfunc residentGitKey(root, head, config string, args []string) (string, bool) {\n\tif config == \"\" {\n\t\t// The effective Git configuration could not be read: nothing is memoized.\n\t\treturn \"\", false\n\t}\n\tgitDir := filepath.Join(root, \".git\")\n\tinfo, err := os.Lstat(gitDir)\n\tif err != nil || !info.IsDir() {\n\t\treturn \"\", false\n\t}\n\t// The shallow file and the repository config are small: their content, not a timestamp,\n\t// is part of the key.\n\tdigestOf := func(name string) string {\n\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(gitDir, name))\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn \"-\"\n\t\t}\n\t\tsum := sha256.Sum256(raw)\n\t\treturn hex.EncodeToString(sum[:8])\n\t}\n\tshallow := digestOf(\"shallow\")\n\t// config is the digest of the effective Git configuration of the root (system, global, user,\n\t// repository, worktree and command-line scopes, includes followed): any of them can change\n\t// what a read answers (log.follow, for one), and the digest is taken once per operation.\n\treturn strings.Join([]string{filepath.Clean(root), head, shallow, config, strings.Join(args, \"\\x00\")}, \"\\x01\"), true\n}\n\nfunc (m *ResidentGitMemo) get(key string) ([]byte, bool) {\n\tm.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer m.mu.Unlock()\n\tel, ok := m.entries[key]\n\tif !ok {\n\t\tm.misses.Add(1)\n\t\treturn nil, false\n\t}\n\tm.order.MoveToFront(el)\n\tm.hits.Add(1)\n\treturn append([]byte(nil), el.Value.(*residentGitEntry).stdout...), true\n}\n\nfunc (m *ResidentGitMemo) put(key string, stdout []byte) {\n\tsize := int64(len(key) + len(stdout))\n\tm.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer m.mu.Unlock()\n\tif size > m.max {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tif el, ok := m.entries[key]; ok {\n\t\tm.bytes -= int64(len(el.Value.(*residentGitEntry).key) + len(el.Value.(*residentGitEntry).stdout))\n\t\tm.order.Remove(el)\n\t\tdelete(m.entries, key)\n\t}\n\tfor m.bytes+size > m.max {\n\t\tlast := m.order.Back()\n\t\tif last == nil {\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t\te := last.Value.(*residentGitEntry)\n\t\tm.bytes -= int64(len(e.key) + len(e.stdout))\n\t\tm.order.Remove(last)\n\t\tdelete(m.entries, e.key)\n\t}\n\tm.entries[key] = m.order.PushFront(&residentGitEntry{key: key, stdout: append([]byte(nil), stdout...)})\n\tm.bytes += size\n}\n","numLines":127,"startLine":1,"totalLines":127}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Y6TF8dGUYgHNCrd9RgcBWt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
