{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LBZcLGDWpmPvPpRf3yyjJC","type":"tool_result","content":"commit 80b49143698e7a4d175456448bad10c6cf9bd993\nAuthor: Oseias Pereira <oseiaspereira88@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Nov 10 16:59:07 2026 -0300\n\n    fix: the resident memo key holds the effective Git configuration; the ADR is accepted for the delivered scope\n    \n    Roadmap review, round 1: the key digested only .git/config and shallow, so a change of the user's, the\n    system's or an included configuration could make a hosted check print what standalone would not; it now\n    holds the digest of git config --list of every scope, read once per operation. The ADR status states\n    what was delivered, the resource-limits draft covers affinity and I/O, and the roadmap is the last\n    change, carrying the trailers of its six member specs.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018BdzfsWLr6Nw1kznrQFvmd\n    POSE-Spec: pose-governance-operation-performance\n    POSE-Spec: pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff\n    POSE-Spec: pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches\n    POSE-Spec: pose-optional-worktree-runtime\n    POSE-Spec: pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache\n    POSE-Spec: pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement\n\ndiff --git a/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md b/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\nindex 5f261301..ac2427a3 100644\n--- a/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\n+++ b/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\n@@ -2,10 +2,14 @@\n \n ## Status\n \n-Proposed — 2026-10-14, for B31/B33/B35; the optional worktree runtime (B35) was delivered in three slices and the delivered state, with where it departs from the decisions above, is the last amendment (2026-11-10). The transport, the identity and the slicing of B35 are decided by the amendment at the end (2026-11-09). No IPC, cache API/schema, daemon lifecycle,\n-platform default or policy is implemented/adopted by this proposal. Reconcile and\n-resolve the structural contract before functional start. Preserve accepted ADRs\n-for active-context discovery, scoped Git readers, obligations and the\n+Accepted for the delivered scope — 2026-11-10 (proposed 2026-10-14, for B31/B33/B35). The\n+optional worktree runtime (B35) was delivered in three slices, each reviewed independently, and\n+the last amendment below states what stands and where it departs from the decisions above:\n+a protected Unix-socket endpoint with identity and handshake, five hosted read checks with typed\n+results, a resident memo of pure Git reads, and admission lanes with a measurement. Not adopted,\n+and needing a spec of their own before they are claimed: CPU quota and affinity, per-command\n+memory and I/O limits, a named pipe for Windows, routing the checks to the runtime by default.\n+Preserve accepted ADRs for active-context discovery, scoped Git readers, obligations and the\n MCP-Conductor-Harness validation boundary.\n \n ## Context\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md\nindex d8d919d6..232fb064 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md\n@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ Fatia 2 da B35 (emenda do ADR de 2026-11-09), reescrita pela medição que as du\n \n ## 2. Requirements\n \n-- R5: O reuso residente guarda só o que é função pura de ids de objeto ou do commit do HEAD nomeado quando a leitura rodou (`governancePureGitRead`), chaveado por raiz, commit, estado raso e comando exato, com budget em bytes e a menos recentemente usada primeiro; fica desligado salvo num processo que o liga (o runtime); um commit novo é um miss; um worktree vinculado não é guardado; os bytes de um hit são admitidos contra o budget da operação como os de uma leitura nova e a auditoria final não aponta mudança.\n+- R5: O reuso residente guarda só o que é função pura de ids de objeto ou do commit do HEAD nomeado quando a leitura rodou (`governancePureGitRead`), chaveado por raiz, commit, estado raso, configuração efetiva do Git (todos os escopos, includes seguidos) e comando exato, com budget em bytes e a menos recentemente usada primeiro; fica desligado salvo num processo que o liga (o runtime); um commit novo é um miss; um worktree vinculado não é guardado; os bytes de um hit são admitidos contra o budget da operação como os de uma leitura nova e a auditoria final não aponta mudança.\n - R7: Um comando hospedado devolve resultado tipado (`outcome` `completed`, `refused`, `deadline` ou `error`, código de saída, saída, época, tempo e acertos do memo); `refused` não iniciou o comando (inclusive o que ainda esperava a sua vez quando o prazo passou, que é retirado e nunca roda depois) e leva ao fallback standalone; `error` é o comando que rodou e terminou com a saída grande demais (acima de 2 MiB) para voltar, com o código de saída dele; `deadline` e uma resposta perdida são `unknown` para o chamador, que não repete o comando e sai com 1 dizendo isso.\n - R10: O runtime só hospeda os cinco checks e só roda um chamador cujo digest de ambiente (variáveis `POSE_`, `HARNE8_`, `GIT_`, `CLAUDE`, `CODEX`, o locale, `HOME`, `NO_COLOR`, o usuário) é o dele; a saída de um comando hospedado é a mesma que ele dá standalone.\n \n@@ -133,6 +133,6 @@ O runtime hospeda `review-check`, `closeout-check`, `artifact-check`, `surface-c\n ### Follow-ups\n \n - [open] Test the admission of a memo hit's bytes against an operation's input budget when the budget is nearly spent. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n-- [open] Put the user and global Git configuration in the memo key, as the repository's own is. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n+- [done] Put the user and global Git configuration in the memo key (the key holds the digest of the effective configuration, read once per operation). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n - [covered: pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement] Admissão, orçamento e proteção das consultas curtas contra checks pesados, com medições fixadas (fatia 3, `pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement`). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2027-02-08)\n - [open] Rotear os checks para o runtime quando ele existe, sem `run` explícito, e renderizar para terminal. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key.md\nindex 9a62562a..72abf97c 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key.md\n@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ O que não está nos requisitos abaixo.\n ## 2. Requirements\n \n - R1: `memo_hits` é contado por operação.\n-- R2: A chave do memo inclui o digest do config global e de usuário do Git.\n+- R2: [withdrawn: a chave do memo passou a conter o digest da configuração efetiva do Git na revisão do roadmap `pose-shared-runtime`, spec `pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache`]\n - R3: Um teste admite um acerto contra um orçamento quase esgotado e vê o recuso do budget.\n \n ## 3. Technical Plan\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command.md\nindex acf7ffa6..7d8231a7 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command.md\n@@ -34,7 +34,8 @@ O que não está nos requisitos abaixo.\n ## 2. Requirements\n \n - R1: Um limite por faixa de CPU e de memória, aplicado onde há cgroup v2, e reportado como efetivo ou não no status.\n-- R2: A medição inclui a CPU e a memória sob o limite e um comando que o excede.\n+- R2: A afinidade de CPU (conjunto de CPUs de cada faixa) e um limite de E/S (`io.max` no cgroup v2) são configuráveis e reportados como efetivos ou não, como a CPU e a memória.\n+- R4: A medição inclui a CPU, a memória e a E/S sob o limite e um comando que o excede.\n - R3: ADR: o limite é do processo do runtime ou de um filho por comando.\n \n ## 3. Technical Plan\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go\nindex 090ed2f5..2d097182 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go\n@@ -42,13 +42,33 @@ type governanceReadViewGitObservation struct {\n // one read-view operation. Repeated commands replay the first result; audit\n // reruns each exact command and reports any changed or unprovable result.\n type governanceReadViewGitState struct {\n-\top           *governanceReadViewOperation\n-\tmu           sync.Mutex\n-\tobservations map[string]*governanceReadViewGitObservation\n+\top            *governanceReadViewOperation\n+\tmu            sync.Mutex\n+\tobservations  map[string]*governanceReadViewGitObservation\n+\tconfigMu      sync.Mutex\n+\tconfigDigests map[string]string\n+}\n+\n+// effectiveGitConfig is the digest of `git config --list` of a root (every scope, includes\n+// followed), read once per operation and kept apart from the command observations: it is a key\n+// of the resident memo, not an input the audit replays. Empty when it could not be read.\n+func (state *governanceReadViewGitState) effectiveGitConfig(ctx context.Context, files Files, root string) string {\n+\tstate.configMu.Lock()\n+\tdefer state.configMu.Unlock()\n+\tif digest, ok := state.configDigests[root]; ok {\n+\t\treturn digest\n+\t}\n+\tdigest := \"\"\n+\tif out, _, err := runGovernanceGitCommandOutputContext(ctx, files, root, []string{\"config\", \"--list\", \"-z\", \"--includes\"}, 1<<20); err == nil {\n+\t\tsum := sha256.Sum256(out)\n+\t\tdigest = hex.EncodeToString(sum[:8])\n+\t}\n+\tstate.configDigests[root] = digest\n+\treturn digest\n }\n \n func newGovernanceReadViewGitState(op *governanceReadViewOperation) *governanceReadViewGitState {\n-\treturn &governanceReadViewGitState{op: op, observations: map[string]*governanceReadViewGitObservation{}}\n+\treturn &governanceReadViewGitState{op: op, observations: map[string]*governanceReadViewGitObservation{}, configDigests: map[string]string{}}\n }\n \n // captureGovernanceGit runs a Git command through the read-view generation\n@@ -340,7 +360,7 @@ func (state *governanceReadViewGitState) capture(files Files, ctx context.Contex\n \tmemoKey, memoized := \"\", false\n \tmemo := residentGit.Load()\n \tif memo != nil && (byObject || byHead && headBefore != \"\") {\n-\t\tif key, ok := residentGitKey(root, headBefore, args); ok {\n+\t\tif key, ok := residentGitKey(root, headBefore, state.effectiveGitConfig(ctx, files, root), args); ok {\n \t\t\tmemoKey = key\n \t\t\tif hit, found := memo.get(key); found {\n \t\t\t\tif int64(len(hit)) > limit || !state.op.reserveInput(int64(len(hit))) {\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo_test.go\nindex 7d39a011..c492cfe3 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo_test.go\n@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@\n package pose\n \n import (\n+\t\"context\"\n \t\"os\"\n \t\"path/filepath\"\n \t\"strings\"\n@@ -19,18 +20,18 @@ func TestTheResidentGitMemoIsOffByDefaultBoundedAndKeyedByTheCommit(t *testing.T\n \tm := EnableResidentGitMemo(400)\n \tdefer DisableResidentGitMemo()\n \targs := []string{\"log\", \"-1\", \"--format=%H\", \"--\", \"a.md\"}\n-\tk1, ok := residentGitKey(root, \"head1\", args)\n+\tk1, ok := residentGitKey(root, \"head1\", \"cfg\", args)\n \tif !ok {\n \t\tt.Fatal(\"a plain .git directory is not memoizable\")\n \t}\n-\tk2, _ := residentGitKey(root, \"head2\", args)\n+\tk2, _ := residentGitKey(root, \"head2\", \"cfg\", args)\n \tif k1 == k2 {\n \t\tt.Fatal(\"two commits share a key\")\n \t}\n \tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"shallow\"), []byte(\"x\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n \t\tt.Fatal(err)\n \t}\n-\tif k3, _ := residentGitKey(root, \"head1\", args); k3 == k1 {\n+\tif k3, _ := residentGitKey(root, \"head1\", \"cfg\", args); k3 == k1 {\n \t\tt.Fatal(\"a shallow repository shares the key of a full one\")\n \t}\n \tm.put(\"a\", []byte(strings.Repeat(\"x\", 150)))\n@@ -52,12 +53,24 @@ func TestTheResidentGitMemoIsOffByDefaultBoundedAndKeyedByTheCommit(t *testing.T\n \tif _, hit := m.get(\"huge\"); hit {\n \t\tt.Fatal(\"an entry larger than the budget was retained\")\n \t}\n+\t// The effective Git configuration is part of the key, and an unreadable one memoizes nothing.\n+\tif os.Remove(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"shallow\")) != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"the shallow file the test wrote is gone\")\n+\t}\n+\tkc1, _ := residentGitKey(root, \"head1\", \"cfgA\", args)\n+\tkc2, _ := residentGitKey(root, \"head1\", \"cfgB\", args)\n+\tif kc1 == kc2 {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"two configurations share a key\")\n+\t}\n+\tif _, ok := residentGitKey(root, \"head1\", \"\", args); ok {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"an unreadable configuration was memoized\")\n+\t}\n \t// A linked worktree (.git is a file) is not memoized.\n \tlinked := t.TempDir()\n \tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(linked, \".git\"), []byte(\"gitdir: elsewhere\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n \t\tt.Fatal(err)\n \t}\n-\tif _, ok := residentGitKey(linked, \"h\", args); ok {\n+\tif _, ok := residentGitKey(linked, \"h\", \"cfg\", args); ok {\n \t\tt.Fatal(\"a linked worktree was memoized\")\n \t}\n }\n@@ -101,3 +114,40 @@ func TestASecondOperationIsAnsweredFromTheMemoAndANewCommitMissesIt(t *testing.T\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"after the new commit hits %d misses %d, want 1 and 2\", hits, misses)\n \t}\n }\n+\n+// A global Git configuration that changes what a read answers must change the key: the digest of\n+// the effective configuration follows a change of the user's own configuration file.\n+func TestTheEffectiveGitConfigurationFollowsTheUsersConfigurationFile(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot := snapshotRepo(t, map[string]string{\"a.md\": \"one\\n\"})\n+\thome := t.TempDir()\n+\tt.Setenv(\"HOME\", home)\n+\tt.Setenv(\"XDG_CONFIG_HOME\", filepath.Join(home, \"xdg\"))\n+\tt.Setenv(\"GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM\", \"1\")\n+\t_, view := (Store{Root: root}).beginGovernanceReadView()\n+\tstate := view.operation.git\n+\tctx := context.Background()\n+\tbefore := state.effectiveGitConfig(ctx, NativeFiles(), root)\n+\tif before == \"\" {\n+\t\tt.Skip(\"the effective Git configuration cannot be read here\")\n+\t}\n+\t// The test process points GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL at a file of its own (testgit.Isolate): that is the\n+\t// user's configuration here.\n+\tuserConfig := os.Getenv(\"GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL\")\n+\tif userConfig == \"\" {\n+\t\tuserConfig = filepath.Join(home, \".gitconfig\")\n+\t}\n+\toriginal, _ := os.ReadFile(userConfig)\n+\tt.Cleanup(func() { _ = os.WriteFile(userConfig, original, 0o644) })\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(userConfig, append(append([]byte(nil), original...), []byte(\"\\n[log]\\n\\tfollow = true\\n\")...), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\t// A new operation reads it again; the same operation keeps the digest it took.\n+\tif same := state.effectiveGitConfig(ctx, NativeFiles(), root); same != before {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"the digest changed inside one operation\")\n+\t}\n+\t_, next := (Store{Root: root}).beginGovernanceReadView()\n+\tafter := next.operation.git.effectiveGitConfig(ctx, NativeFiles(), root)\n+\tif after == before {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"a change of the user's Git configuration did not change the key\")\n+\t}\n+}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"9a4bfc7b-f53a-4cc8-a09d-4fbe0fc94a75","timestamp":"2026-11-10T20:53:39.091Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"commit 80b49143698e7a4d175456448bad10c6cf9bd993\nAuthor: Oseias Pereira <oseiaspereira88@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Nov 10 16:59:07 2026 -0300\n\n    fix: the resident memo key holds the effective Git configuration; the ADR is accepted for the delivered scope\n    \n    Roadmap review, round 1: the key digested only .git/config and shallow, so a change of the user's, the\n    system's or an included configuration could make a hosted check print what standalone would not; it now\n    holds the digest of git config --list of every scope, read once per operation. The ADR status states\n    what was delivered, the resource-limits draft covers affinity and I/O, and the roadmap is the last\n    change, carrying the trailers of its six member specs.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018BdzfsWLr6Nw1kznrQFvmd\n    POSE-Spec: pose-governance-operation-performance\n    POSE-Spec: pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff\n    POSE-Spec: pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches\n    POSE-Spec: pose-optional-worktree-runtime\n    POSE-Spec: pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache\n    POSE-Spec: pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement\n\ndiff --git a/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md b/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\nindex 5f261301..ac2427a3 100644\n--- a/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\n+++ b/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\n@@ -2,10 +2,14 @@\n \n ## Status\n \n-Proposed — 2026-10-14, for B31/B33/B35; the optional worktree runtime (B35) was delivered in three slices and the delivered state, with where it departs from the decisions above, is the last amendment (2026-11-10). The transport, the identity and the slicing of B35 are decided by the amendment at the end (2026-11-09). No IPC, cache API/schema, daemon lifecycle,\n-platform default or policy is implemented/adopted by this proposal. Reconcile and\n-resolve the structural contract before functional start. Preserve accepted ADRs\n-for active-context discovery, scoped Git readers, obligations and the\n+Accepted for the delivered scope — 2026-11-10 (proposed 2026-10-14, for B31/B33/B35). The\n+optional worktree runtime (B35) was delivered in three slices, each reviewed independently, and\n+the last amendment below states what stands and where it departs from the decisions above:\n+a protected Unix-socket endpoint with identity and handshake, five hosted read checks with typed\n+results, a resident memo of pure Git reads, and admission lanes with a measurement. Not adopted,\n+and needing a spec of their own before they are claimed: CPU quota and affinity, per-command\n+memory and I/O limits, a named pipe for Windows, routing the checks to the runtime by default.\n+Preserve accepted ADRs for active-context discovery, scoped Git readers, obligations and the\n MCP-Conductor-Harness validation boundary.\n \n ## Context\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md\nindex d8d919d6..232fb064 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache.md\n@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ Fatia 2 da B35 (emenda do ADR de 2026-11-09), reescrita pela medição que as du\n \n ## 2. Requirements\n \n-- R5: O reuso residente guarda só o que é função pura de ids de objeto ou do commit do HEAD nomeado quando a leitura rodou (`governancePureGitRead`), chaveado por raiz, commit, estado raso e comando exato, com budget em bytes e a menos recentemente usada primeiro; fica desligado salvo num processo que o liga (o runtime); um commit novo é um miss; um worktree vinculado não é guardado; os bytes de um hit são admitidos contra o budget da operação como os de uma leitura nova e a auditoria final não aponta mudança.\n+- R5: O reuso residente guarda só o que é função pura de ids de objeto ou do commit do HEAD nomeado quando a leitura rodou (`governancePureGitRead`), chaveado por raiz, commit, estado raso, configuração efetiva do Git (todos os escopos, includes seguidos) e comando exato, com budget em bytes e a menos recentemente usada primeiro; fica desligado salvo num processo que o liga (o runtime); um commit novo é um miss; um worktree vinculado não é guardado; os bytes de um hit são admitidos contra o budget da operação como os de uma leitura nova e a auditoria final não aponta mudança.\n - R7: Um comando hospedado devolve resultado tipado (`outcome` `completed`, `refused`, `deadline` ou `error`, código de saída, saída, época, tempo e acertos do memo); `refused` não iniciou o comando (inclusive o que ainda esperava a sua vez quando o prazo passou, que é retirado e nunca roda depois) e leva ao fallback standalone; `error` é o comando que rodou e terminou com a saída grande demais (acima de 2 MiB) para voltar, com o código de saída dele; `deadline` e uma resposta perdida são `unknown` para o chamador, que não repete o comando e sai com 1 dizendo isso.\n - R10: O runtime só hospeda os cinco checks e só roda um chamador cujo digest de ambiente (variáveis `POSE_`, `HARNE8_`, `GIT_`, `CLAUDE`, `CODEX`, o locale, `HOME`, `NO_COLOR`, o usuário) é o dele; a saída de um comando hospedado é a mesma que ele dá standalone.\n \n@@ -133,6 +133,6 @@ O runtime hospeda `review-check`, `closeout-check`, `artifact-check`, `surface-c\n ### Follow-ups\n \n - [open] Test the admission of a memo hit's bytes against an operation's input budget when the budget is nearly spent. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n-- [open] Put the user and global Git configuration in the memo key, as the repository's own is. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n+- [done] Put the user and global Git configuration in the memo key (the key holds the digest of the effective configuration, read once per operation). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\n - [covered: pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement] Admissão, orçamento e proteção das consultas curtas contra checks pesados, com medições fixadas (fatia 3, `pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement`). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2027-02-08)\n - [open] Rotear os checks para o runtime quando ele existe, sem `run` explícito, e renderizar para terminal. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2027-02-08)\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key.md\nindex 9a62562a..72abf97c 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key.md\n@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ O que não está nos requisitos abaixo.\n ## 2. Requirements\n \n - R1: `memo_hits` é contado por operação.\n-- R2: A chave do memo inclui o digest do config global e de usuário do Git.\n+- R2: [withdrawn: a chave do memo passou a conter o digest da configuração efetiva do Git na revisão do roadmap `pose-shared-runtime`, spec `pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache`]\n - R3: Um teste admite um acerto contra um orçamento quase esgotado e vê o recuso do budget.\n \n ## 3. Technical Plan\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command.md\nindex acf7ffa6..7d8231a7 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command.md\n@@ -34,7 +34,8 @@ O que não está nos requisitos abaixo.\n ## 2. Requirements\n \n - R1: Um limite por faixa de CPU e de memória, aplicado onde há cgroup v2, e reportado como efetivo ou não no status.\n-- R2: A medição inclui a CPU e a memória sob o limite e um comando que o excede.\n+- R2: A afinidade de CPU (conjunto de CPUs de cada faixa) e um limite de E/S (`io.max` no cgroup v2) são configuráveis e reportados como efetivos ou não, como a CPU e a memória.\n+- R4: A medição inclui a CPU, a memória e a E/S sob o limite e um comando que o excede.\n - R3: ADR: o limite é do processo do runtime ou de um filho por comando.\n \n ## 3. Technical Plan\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go\nindex 090ed2f5..2d097182 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go\n@@ -42,13 +42,33 @@ type governanceReadViewGitObservation struct {\n // one read-view operation. Repeated commands replay the first result; audit\n // reruns each exact command and reports any changed or unprovable result.\n type governanceReadViewGitState struct {\n-\top           *governanceReadViewOperation\n-\tmu           sync.Mutex\n-\tobservations map[string]*governanceReadViewGitObservation\n+\top            *governanceReadViewOperation\n+\tmu            sync.Mutex\n+\tobservations  map[string]*governanceReadViewGitObservation\n+\tconfigMu      sync.Mutex\n+\tconfigDigests map[string]string\n+}\n+\n+// effectiveGitConfig is the digest of `git config --list` of a root (every scope, includes\n+// followed), read once per operation and kept apart from the command observations: it is a key\n+// of the resident memo, not an input the audit replays. Empty when it could not be read.\n+func (state *governanceReadViewGitState) effectiveGitConfig(ctx context.Context, files Files, root string) string {\n+\tstate.configMu.Lock()\n+\tdefer state.configMu.Unlock()\n+\tif digest, ok := state.configDigests[root]; ok {\n+\t\treturn digest\n+\t}\n+\tdigest := \"\"\n+\tif out, _, err := runGovernanceGitCommandOutputContext(ctx, files, root, []string{\"config\", \"--list\", \"-z\", \"--includes\"}, 1<<20); err == nil {\n+\t\tsum := sha256.Sum256(out)\n+\t\tdigest = hex.EncodeToString(sum[:8])\n+\t}\n+\tstate.configDigests[root] = digest\n+\treturn digest\n }\n \n func newGovernanceReadViewGitState(op *governanceReadViewOperation) *governanceReadViewGitState {\n-\treturn &governanceReadViewGitState{op: op, observations: map[string]*governanceReadViewGitObservation{}}\n+\treturn &governanceReadViewGitState{op: op, observations: map[string]*governanceReadViewGitObservation{}, configDigests: map[string]string{}}\n }\n \n // captureGovernanceGit runs a Git command through the read-view generation\n@@ -340,7 +360,7 @@ func (state *governanceReadViewGitState) capture(files Files, ctx context.Contex\n \tmemoKey, memoized := \"\", false\n \tmemo := residentGit.Load()\n \tif memo != nil && (byObject || byHead && headBefore != \"\") {\n-\t\tif key, ok := residentGitKey(root, headBefore, args); ok {\n+\t\tif key, ok := residentGitKey(root, headBefore, state.effectiveGitConfig(ctx, files, root), args); ok {\n \t\t\tmemoKey = key\n \t\t\tif hit, found := memo.get(key); found {\n \t\t\t\tif int64(len(hit)) > limit || !state.op.reserveInput(int64(len(hit))) {\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo_test.go\nindex 7d39a011..c492cfe3 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo_test.go\n@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@\n package pose\n \n import (\n+\t\"context\"\n \t\"os\"\n \t\"path/filepath\"\n \t\"strings\"\n@@ -19,18 +20,18 @@ func TestTheResidentGitMemoIsOffByDefaultBoundedAndKeyedByTheCommit(t *testing.T\n \tm := EnableResidentGitMemo(400)\n \tdefer DisableResidentGitMemo()\n \targs := []string{\"log\", \"-1\", \"--format=%H\", \"--\", \"a.md\"}\n-\tk1, ok := residentGitKey(root, \"head1\", args)\n+\tk1, ok := residentGitKey(root, \"head1\", \"cfg\", args)\n \tif !ok {\n \t\tt.Fatal(\"a plain .git directory is not memoizable\")\n \t}\n-\tk2, _ := residentGitKey(root, \"head2\", args)\n+\tk2, _ := residentGitKey(root, \"head2\", \"cfg\", args)\n \tif k1 == k2 {\n \t\tt.Fatal(\"two commits share a key\")\n \t}\n \tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"shallow\"), []byte(\"x\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n \t\tt.Fatal(err)\n \t}\n-\tif k3, _ := residentGitKey(root, \"head1\", args); k3 == k1 {\n+\tif k3, _ := residentGitKey(root, \"head1\", \"cfg\", args); k3 == k1 {\n \t\tt.Fatal(\"a shallow repository shares the key of a full one\")\n \t}\n \tm.put(\"a\", []byte(strings.Repeat(\"x\", 150)))\n@@ -52,12 +53,24 @@ func TestTheResidentGitMemoIsOffByDefaultBoundedAndKeyedByTheCommit(t *testing.T\n \tif _, hit := m.get(\"huge\"); hit {\n \t\tt.Fatal(\"an entry larger than the budget was retained\")\n \t}\n+\t// The effective Git configuration is part of the key, and an unreadable one memoizes nothing.\n+\tif os.Remove(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"shallow\")) != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"the shallow file the test wrote is gone\")\n+\t}\n+\tkc1, _ := residentGitKey(root, \"head1\", \"cfgA\", args)\n+\tkc2, _ := residentGitKey(root, \"head1\", \"cfgB\", args)\n+\tif kc1 == kc2 {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"two configurations share a key\")\n+\t}\n+\tif _, ok := residentGitKey(root, \"head1\", \"\", args); ok {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"an unreadable configuration was memoized\")\n+\t}\n \t// A linked worktree (.git is a file) is not memoized.\n \tlinked := t.TempDir()\n \tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(linked, \".git\"), []byte(\"gitdir: elsewhere\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n \t\tt.Fatal(err)\n \t}\n-\tif _, ok := residentGitKey(linked, \"h\", args); ok {\n+\tif _, ok := residentGitKey(linked, \"h\", \"cfg\", args); ok {\n \t\tt.Fatal(\"a linked worktree was memoized\")\n \t}\n }\n@@ -101,3 +114,40 @@ func TestASecondOperationIsAnsweredFromTheMemoAndANewCommitMissesIt(t *testing.T\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"after the new commit hits %d misses %d, want 1 and 2\", hits, misses)\n \t}\n }\n+\n+// A global Git configuration that changes what a read answers must change the key: the digest of\n+// the effective configuration follows a change of the user's own configuration file.\n+func TestTheEffectiveGitConfigurationFollowsTheUsersConfigurationFile(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot := snapshotRepo(t, map[string]string{\"a.md\": \"one\\n\"})\n+\thome := t.TempDir()\n+\tt.Setenv(\"HOME\", home)\n+\tt.Setenv(\"XDG_CONFIG_HOME\", filepath.Join(home, \"xdg\"))\n+\tt.Setenv(\"GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM\", \"1\")\n+\t_, view := (Store{Root: root}).beginGovernanceReadView()\n+\tstate := view.operation.git\n+\tctx := context.Background()\n+\tbefore := state.effectiveGitConfig(ctx, NativeFiles(), root)\n+\tif before == \"\" {\n+\t\tt.Skip(\"the effective Git configuration cannot be read here\")\n+\t}\n+\t// The test process points GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL at a file of its own (testgit.Isolate): that is the\n+\t// user's configuration here.\n+\tuserConfig := os.Getenv(\"GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL\")\n+\tif userConfig == \"\" {\n+\t\tuserConfig = filepath.Join(home, \".gitconfig\")\n+\t}\n+\toriginal, _ := os.ReadFile(userConfig)\n+\tt.Cleanup(func() { _ = os.WriteFile(userConfig, original, 0o644) })\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(userConfig, append(append([]byte(nil), original...), []byte(\"\\n[log]\\n\\tfollow = true\\n\")...), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\t// A new operation reads it again; the same operation keeps the digest it took.\n+\tif same := state.effectiveGitConfig(ctx, NativeFiles(), root); same != before {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"the digest changed inside one operation\")\n+\t}\n+\t_, next := (Store{Root: root}).beginGovernanceReadView()\n+\tafter := next.operation.git.effectiveGitConfig(ctx, NativeFiles(), root)\n+\tif after == before {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"a change of the user's Git configuration did not change the key\")\n+\t}\n+}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LBZcLGDWpmPvPpRf3yyjJC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
