{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cguut7auPa1LPuSFPfuzG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**decision: approved.** The code and documents support approval. One caveat matters more than the verdict: the two required `validate` tools could not be run, so POSE will likely refuse this draft under rule (g).\n\n## What I could not do\n\nThe profile refused every plan-tool command I tried (`pose roadmap-check pose-shared-runtime --strict`, `pose validate --strict --module scripts`). Only `git status` ran. As a result:\n\n- **`validate [pose-mcp]` and `validate [scripts]`:** these name no evidence class, so they need a `command:` I actually ran. I didn't run them, so I've marked them `deferred` rather than claim a pass. To get a recordable conclusion, re-run this review with a profile that allows `pose validate`.\n- **`roadmap-check` and `assess-integrate`:** these accept integration evidence, so I've cited the sealed refs and said in the rationale that my own run was refused.\n\n## Previous findings\n\n- **R1-F1 — fixed.** The memo key now includes a digest of `git config --list -z --includes` (`resident_git_memo.go:62-86`). That digest is read once per operation per root, through the same Git call the reads use (`governance_read_view_git.go:51-68`), and passed in at `:363`. If the config can't be read, nothing is memoized (`:63-66`). New tests cover two configs giving two keys, an unreadable config, and a change to the user's config file. Spec R5 was updated, and the draft spec's R2 was withdrawn.\n- **R1-F2 — not fixed.** `runtime_host.go:134,145` are unchanged. It is still low and tracked in draft `pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key` R1. I carry it forward as N2 so it can be accepted as a risk.\n- **R1-F3 — fixed.** The ADR status (`:5-13`) now reads \"Accepted for the delivered scope\" and lists what was and wasn't adopted.\n- **R1-F4 — fixed.** `pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command.md:37-38` now covers CPU affinity, `io.max`, and measuring I/O.\n\n## New finding\n\n- **N1 (low)** at `.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:298-299`: the amendment's Caches bullet still says the key is \"the content of the shallow file and of the repository config\". It should now say the effective Git configuration.\n\n## Criteria\n\n- **cross-component-integration — passed:** the shared CLI/MCP operation and route inventory have passing integration evidence.\n- **cut-criteria — passed:** each exit gate (B32, B31, B33, B35) has passing integration evidence, and every non-delivered item is either in a draft spec or explicitly marked \"not delivered\" in the ADR.\n- **end-to-end — passed:** `pose runtime run` covers hosted run, typed results, refusal, standalone fallback and the deadline-unknown case (`runtime_host.go:100-165`).\n- **milestones — passed:** all four milestones list closed member specs.\n- **outcome — passed:** coherent operations, cost per producer, bounded reuse, and a runtime that stays opt-in with standalone kept.\n- **release-readiness — finding (N1):** the stale ADR sentence.\n- **residual-risk — passed:** only low findings remain, each with an owner and a review date.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"N1\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \".pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\", \"line\": 298, \"summary\": \"The 2026-11-10 amendment's Caches bullet says the resident memo is keyed by the content of the shallow file and of the repository config; after the R1-F1 fix the key holds the digest of the effective Git configuration (all scopes, includes followed), so the ADR misdescribes the delivered key.\", \"action\": \"Update the Caches bullet of the 2026-11-10 ADR amendment to name the effective Git configuration digest as part of the key.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go\", \"line\": 134, \"summary\": \"Carried from R1-F2 (not fixed): memo_hits is the difference of the process-global hit counter read before (134) and after (145) the command, so with concurrent lanes it includes other commands' hits; tracked as R1 of draft spec pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key.\", \"action\": \"Count memo hits per operation (draft spec pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key R1).\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"}\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F1\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go:62-86 adds the effective-config digest to the key and refuses to memoize when it is empty; governance_read_view_git.go:51-68 effectiveGitConfig reads `git config --list -z --includes` once per operation per root through the same Git invocation as the reads, wired at :363; resident_git_memo_test.go TestTheEffectiveGitConfigurationFollowsTheUsersConfigurationFile and the cfgA/cfgB and empty-config assertions; spec pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache R5 updated (git show HEAD).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F2\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:134 and :145 still diff the global ResidentGitMemoStats counter; carried as N2 (low follow-up), tracked in draft spec pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key R1.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F3\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \".pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:5-13 status now 'Accepted for the delivered scope — 2026-11-10' listing delivered and not-adopted items; the 'no IPC ... implemented' sentence is removed.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F4\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command.md:37 (R2: CPU affinity per lane and io.max I/O limit, reported effective or not) and :38 (R4: measurement includes I/O).\"}\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Last commit 80b49143 diff (ADR, roadmap, member and draft specs, governance_read_view_git.go, resident_git_memo.go and test); resident memo key construction, lock order (state.mu then configMu) and the hit/budget path in capture (governance_read_view_git.go:330-418) and the Git invocation used for the config read (:598-629); runtime host admission, lanes, deadline and orphan accounting and memo_hits (runtime_host.go:100-165); roadmap outcome, Estado paragraph and four milestone exit gates; ADR status and 2026-11-10 amendment; draft specs pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command, pose-runtime-windows-named-pipe, pose-checks-route-to-the-runtime-by-default, pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key; sealed evidence list. Plan tool execution (pose roadmap-check, pose validate) was denied by the session profile; only git status ran.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"cross-component-integration\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the shared common operation (pose/common_operation.go, cli/common_operation_register.go) and the MCP route inventory; the CLI/MCP handoff boundary is covered by sealed integration evidence that passed, together with cli-mcp-operation-results-integration and optional-worktree-runtime-integration.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"cut-criteria\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Checked each exit gate in .pose/roadmaps/pose-shared-runtime.md against sealed integration evidence: B32 governance-operation-performance-integration, B31 common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration, B33 bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration, B35 optional-worktree-runtime/resident-cache/runtime-qos-integration. The non-delivered CPU quota/affinity, per-command limits, Windows pipe and default routing are declared in the roadmap and ADR and each sits in its own draft spec.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"end-to-end\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Read the user path pose runtime run -> handshake/identity -> lane admission -> hosted mainCommand -> typed reply, including refused-to-standalone fallback and deadline-is-unknown-not-retried (runtime_host.go:100-165, cmdRuntimeRun); the sealed integration evidence for the runtime and resident cache passed.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"milestones\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The roadmap lists four milestones whose member specs (six) are closed and carried as trailers on the last commit; each milestone's integration evidence is sealed and passing. Per the brief, the review records themselves are not in this checkout, and I judged the roadmap state.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"outcome\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-operation-performance-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The outcome (coherent CLI/MCP operations, controlled cost per producer, bounded reuse, an optional runtime only after identity, coherence, authorization and recovery are qualified) is met: the runtime is opt-in with standalone fallback, the memo is bounded and now keyed by the effective Git config, and its departures are disclosed in the ADR amendment.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"release-readiness\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"N1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"residual-risk\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/resident-cache-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The medium blocker R1-F1 is fixed. The remaining items (N1, N2/R1-F2) are low follow-ups with action, owner and review date, and the non-delivered scope is in draft specs. No undisposed blocking risk remains.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; the session profile denied running pose commands.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"scripts\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; the session profile denied running pose commands.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Relied on sealed integration evidence; my own invocation was denied by the session profile.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; the session profile denied running pose commands.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"roadmap-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Relied on sealed integration evidence; my invocation of pose roadmap-check pose-shared-runtime --strict was denied by the session profile.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; the session profile denied running pose commands.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"scripts\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended; the session profile denied running pose commands.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Not run: the session profile denied pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp, and this tool names no evidence class, so no sealed ref can stand in for a command I ran.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"